@startsalt
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' Sibling of choice-prompt-render.puml, which owns the gating logic and the prose.
' This file owns only the resolved layout: what the operator confronts once
' applicableRows, comingSoon, gateAddons and gateEvidence have already executed.
'
' The checkboxes are grouped into two PLANES, each named by its own divider:
' execution (where the agent runs) and interface (what it can drive). One
' undifferentiated "add-ons" row put a Docker daemon beside a browser as though
' they answered the same question, and named only the first group because the
' divider was inferred from "the first multi-select row" rather than declared.
' Source: internal/choiceui/choiceui.go draw(); cmd/proveo/main.go row builders.
'
' Salt possesses no conditional construct. Optionality is consequently encoded,
' never branched — the five encodings are demonstrated below and named in the
' legend. The variant that eliminates the form entirely (no TTY) has no frame.
'
' The models row shows the BRIDGE OUTPUT, not the role vars the operator set.
' defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh maps ARCHITECT_MODEL (falling back to
' EDITOR_MODEL) into ANTHROPIC_MODEL, and SMALL_MODEL into
' ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL — two slots, so a third role var is never read.
' Bridge dialects for the other harnesses: _spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml.
'
' PLANNED, not drawn here: a topology strip under the hints.
'   the mechanism ..... _spec/_plans/choiceui-topology-animation.puml
'   where it fits ..... _spec/_plans/choiceui-viewport-proposals.puml
'   every frame ....... _spec/_plans/choiceui-animation-states.puml
' Nothing in those three has shipped; this file stays the resolved layout of today.

title Choice prompt wireframe — resolved layout, and how a gated element is drawn

{
{+
  {
    <&terminal> proveo SOLUTIONS | proveo/sandbox: portable, safe AI coding agents
  }
  ==run claudecode — confirm or change this run
  {
    git: | monorepo on <color:#00BAC6>rs-295-integration-discriminator</color> <i>(uncommitted changes)</i>
    keys: | ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
    tooling: | node  nx  python  docker
    lsp: | <color:#00BAC6><&code></color> typescript-language-server  <color:#00BAC6><&code></color> pyright-langserver  <color:#00BAC6><&terminal></color> bash-language-server  <color:#00BAC6><&box></color> docker-langserver  <color:#00BAC6><&document></color> yaml-language-server
    subagents: | 7 definition(s)
    hooks: | .claude/settings.json
    llms: | <color:#00BAC6>main=claude-opus-5 (anthropic)</color>   <color:#00BAC6>small=claude-haiku-4-5 (anthropic)</color>
  }
  ~~
  {
    . | ◀ riskier | . | safer ▶ | .
    ▸ egress | (X) open | ( ) allowlist | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>review | <color:#9a9a9a>— review: not supported on the docker sandbox backend
    credentials | (X) forward | ( ) broker | . | .
    . | . | ———— execution ———— | . | .
    . | [ ] <color:#9a9a9a>host</color> | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>docker (sandbox)</color> | . | .
    . | . | ———— interface ———— | . | .
    . | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui (this session)</color> | [X] browser | [ ] <color:#9a9a9a>chrome (host browser) | <color:#9a9a9a>— chrome (host browser): docker backend only — set…
    agent evidence | [ ] default | [X] verbose | . | .
  }
  --
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel
  ..
  always on: every run on this harness is sandboxed — set PROVEO_SBX=0 to fall back to the docker backend
}
{
{^"1 · greyed — comingSoon"
  egress | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>review | <color:#9a9a9a>— needs a local docker daemon
  .
  Rendered, never selectable. The cursor
  vacates it and the violated constraint
  is named in place, so an unimplemented
  tier is not misread as nonexistent.
}
{^"2 · empty cell — option withdrawn"
  egress | (X) open | ( ) allowlist | .
  .
  The slot persists, so surviving options
  retain the column they occupied while
  the full complement was offered.
}
{^"3 · absent region — applicableRows"
  . | ◀ riskier | . | safer ▶
  egress | (X) open | ( ) allowlist | .
  .
  An axis with nothing to determine is
  eliminated wholesale. The legend
  survives while one ordered row remains.
}
{^"4 · struck — cleared by a gate"
  before | [ ] default | [X] verbose
  after | [X] default | [ ] <s><color:#9a9a9a>verbose</color></s>
  .
  Activation deactivates the counterpart.
  Simultaneous deactivation is permissible
  and signifies "default".
}
{^"5 · filtered — the bridge never reads it"
  set by operator | <color:#00BAC6>ARCHITECT_MODEL</color> | <color:#9a9a9a><s>EDITOR_MODEL</s></color> | <color:#00BAC6>SMALL_MODEL</color>
  claudecode reads | <color:#00BAC6>ANTHROPIC_MODEL</color> | . | <color:#00BAC6>ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL</color>
  prompt shows | <color:#00BAC6>main=</color> | . | <color:#00BAC6>small=</color>
  .
  Claude Code routes internally and exposes two slots, so ""EDITOR_MODEL"" is a
  fallback that never fires once ""ARCHITECT_MODEL"" is set. Printing all three
  role vars advertises an assignment the harness cannot honour, so the header
  shows the resolved slots instead — and every slot it shows is highlighted,
  because a half-highlighted row reads as one model mattering more than another.
}
{^"7 · described — the cursor's option explains itself, BELOW the hint"
  interface | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui (this session)</color> | [X] browser | [ ] <color:#9a9a9a>chrome (host browser)</color>
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel | . | . | .
  <color:#00BAC6>› chrome (host browser) — your own Chrome, with your profile and logins,</color> | . | . | .
  <color:#9a9a9a>off: Claude Code disables it for CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN sessions</color> | . | . | .
  .
  The picker could only ever explain what it had taken AWAY: ""Reason"" is written
  when an option is gated off, so the add-ons that were available and ticked
  carried no text at all and "browser" had to be inferred from its name.
  ""Help"" describes the option the CURSOR is on, one row at a time — describing
  every option of every row at once is the wall of text this replaces.

  WRAPPED, never appended to the row: the row is already ~70 columns of
  checkboxes, so text placed after them runs off the terminal, which is how the
  one description the picker did have ended mid-sentence. The row's own
  ""Reason"" is still drawn inline and is now clipped with an ellipsis — it is a
  glance signal for a row the cursor is not on, and the same words are here in
  full.

  **Pinned LAST, under the hint, with nothing drawn after it.** Under its own row
  the block's height changed with the cursor and shoved every row beneath it up
  and down — the form moved while the operator was reading it. At the bottom it
  can grow freely and nothing above ever shifts.

  A greyed box that is TICKED reads "always on:" rather than "off:": it is not
  unavailable, it is compulsory, and the other label would say the opposite of
  what the checkbox shows.
}
{^"8 · fixed — a box that states a fact"
  execution | [ ] <color:#9a9a9a>host</color> | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>docker (sandbox)</color> | .
  interface | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui (this session)</color> | [X] browser | .
  .
  Greyed, and left in the state it states. ""host"" is the alternative an operator
  might otherwise assume unticking the daemon selects — it never is, because
  proveo containerises every run — and the TUI is the interface for the whole
  session whether or not a browser joins it. Neither is reported as a selected
  add-on, and neither appears in the row's inline ""Reason"": a note greyed on
  every run teaches the operator to skip the line that sometimes matters.

  **The sandbox is greyed for the opposite reason: it is COMPULSORY.** A harness
  that declares sbx runs there and nowhere else, so the box is ticked and locked
  and its help line reads "always on:". Unticking used to reach the docker
  backend behind egress sidecars — a weaker boundary one keystroke away — and
  that escape is now ""PROVEO_SBX=0"", which the greyed reason names. Like the
  two facts above it stays out of the row's inline ""Reason"": a note greyed on
  every run only teaches the operator to skip the line that sometimes matters.

  It is the one greyed box that IS reported as a selected add-on. ""Selections""
  drops every greyed option, which is right for the two facts above and wrong
  here: a compulsory sandbox dropped from the read-back would send the run to
  the very backend the lock exists to remove.
}
{^"6 · nerd, fallback ascii — PROVEO_GLYPHS"
  default (nerd) | <&code> typescript-language-server | <&terminal> bash-language-server
  ""=ascii"" | <> typescript-language-server | $ bash-language-server
  ""=off"" | typescript-language-server | bash-language-server
  .
  Devicons live in a range a Powerline-patched font does not carry, and a terminal
  cannot be asked whether its font holds a codepoint — so nerd is the default and
  ""ascii"" is the fallback an operator selects, never one autodetection guesses.
  ASCII markers are category-level (""<>"" code, ""$"" shell, ""#"" container,
  ""{}"" data) because a decoded symbol cannot carry per-language identity, and they
  avoid ""["", ""("" and "">"", which the checkbox, radio and legend already own.
}
}
}

legend bottom
  <color:#9a9a9a>grey text</color> — offered, never selectable; the violated constraint is drawn on the row
  a "." cell — element absent, column position preserved for the survivors
  a titled group box — region rendered only while its title predicate holds
  <s>struck</s> — cleared by a cross-row gate, or never read by this harness
  no frame whatsoever — no TTY, so the form is never drawn and resolved values stand
  a glyph before a label — accented marker; devicon by default, ASCII via PROVEO_GLYPHS=ascii
  a "›" line under a row — what the option the cursor is on does, wrapped; "off:" adds why it cannot be picked
end legend
@endsalt
